WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.410
- [Interviewer] All right, Lee.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.300
Lee, where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.470
Where you from originally?

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.230
- [Lee] Originally from Dayton, Tennessee,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.767
right between Nashville and Chattanooga.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:13.600
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your family.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.600
You had both of your
parents when you were young?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.820
- Yeah, I lost my mom when I was nine.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.693
I lost my dad when I was 17.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.104
- [Interviewer] And how would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:22.104 --> 00:00:22.937
- Huh?

00:00:22.937 --> 00:00:26.440
- [Interviewer] How would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.380
- We didn't have much.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.080
We were a poor family.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.530
I wouldn't say completely poor,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.740
but mostly-

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.260
- [Interviewer] That whole
region is fairly poor.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:40.260
- Yeah, mostly blackland
farmer is what they call 'em.

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:41.530
- [Interviewer] What
is a blackland farmer?

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.310
- Where they do farm work off and on,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.743
here and there for people.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.360
- [Interviewer] And any abuse?

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.430
Any kind of craziness in your childhood?

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.263
- None.

00:00:52.263 --> 00:00:53.230
- Nothing?
- Uh huh.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.970
- [Interviewer] And how
far did you go in school?

00:00:55.970 --> 00:01:00.970
- I lacked three weeks to
finish the seventh grade.

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:02.000
- [Interviewer] And
that's as far as you went?

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.940
- Yeah, 'cause they was
passing me on D's and F's.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.990
I never didn't do that
good in school anyhow.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.810
I failed the first grade,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:09.993
and I failed the sixth,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.333
and I quit in the seventh.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.380
- [Interviewer] What'd you do after that?

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.630
- What'd I do after that?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.670
Well, I went and registered for the Army,

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.810
but they turned me down

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.330
'cause they classified me as A,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.910
but then never went for my exam,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.593
they classified me as 4-F.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.610
And so, after that,

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.070
I just, whatever kind
of work I could pick up,

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.020
that's what I done.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.380
In other words, I'm a Jack of all trades

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.543
and a master of none.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:41.110
- [Interviewer] And then,
do you have any kids?

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.200
Ever married?

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.520
- Yes, I've been married twice.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.303
I've got three kids.

00:01:47.388 --> 00:01:49.400
Two kids by the first wife,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.053
I got one kid out of wedlock that's mine.

00:01:55.832 --> 00:01:58.080
And then I had, my second marriage,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.463
I had four stepdaughters.

00:02:02.536 --> 00:02:04.070
- [Interviewer] And then at
some point you got in trouble

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:05.803
with the law?

00:02:05.803 --> 00:02:08.673
- Yeah, in 1984.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.570
You see, me and the old
lady would have been married

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.040
for about, me and my first wife,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.863
been married about 14, 15 years.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.230
Let's see, my first child
with her was born in April of

00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:28.360
'74.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.087
And my son was born in '76.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.180
And after my son was born,

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.013
me and the wife,

00:02:34.013 --> 00:02:35.463
we didn't have sex or nothing.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.200
She cut me off completely.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.860
I used to drink a lot.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.760
I put that all down in '67.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.583
Oh wait, '97 really.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.720
I put it all down, quit it all

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.267
September the 21st of '97.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.153
And

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:58.680
my wife, she decided one day,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.710
she wanted a divorce.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.543
I told her, I said,

00:03:00.543 --> 00:03:01.380
"Well, whenever I married you,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.977
I didn't marry you to give you no divorce.

00:03:02.977 --> 00:03:05.300
"Well, I'll get it one way or the other!"

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.780
And so that's when I was accused

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.123
of messing with my daughter and my niece.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.990
And that's whenever I started

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.530
getting in trouble with the law then.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.313
DUIs, I had a few of them.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:21.113
Because I used to drink
a lot back, years ago.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:22.973
And just like I said,

00:03:22.973 --> 00:03:24.227
I put it all down in '97

00:03:24.227 --> 00:03:25.570
and ain't touched it sense.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.403
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:03:26.403 --> 00:03:30.163
And the incidents with the kids,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.430
that was something that
actually happened or?

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.910
- No, she accused me of it
'cause she wanted a divorce.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.780
That's how she got her divorce.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.750
- [Interviewer] So, you
claim it never happened?

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.860
- Nope, it never happened.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.450
I mean, somebody did
mess with my daughter.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.153
The fella that did mess with her,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.180
he died while I was locked up.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.970
- [Interviewer] How many
years in prison did you do?

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.230
- I done 15 years in prison.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.984
19 years at Arcadia,

00:03:59.984 --> 00:04:03.733
at what you you call it?

00:04:05.553 --> 00:04:06.386
- [Interviewer] Was that therapy?

00:04:06.386 --> 00:04:08.080
- Yeah, therapy.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.523
19 years in there.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.060
- [Interviewer] So a total of-

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.557
- 37.

00:04:13.557 --> 00:04:17.963
37, 38 that I've been locked up. (coughs)

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.560
- [Interviewer] And looking
back at all of that,

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.590
how do you view all that?

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.590
Do you feel like you just got robbed or?

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.900
- Well no, I feel that I got
cheated out of a marriage,

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:32.990
out of my kids.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.437
I ain't seen them since '84.

00:04:34.437 --> 00:04:36.720
- [Interviewer] I mean 37
years in prison is rough.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.670
- Yeah, it is.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.513
It sure is.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.430
- [Interviewer] And
for something you claim

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.730
you are innocent of that makes it tough.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:44.563
- But just like I said,

00:04:44.563 --> 00:04:47.070
the fellow that did mess with her,

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:48.600
and if she would've said something to me,

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.980
I'd have took care of it
'cause that's the way I do.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.763
I take care of my family, you know?

00:04:55.306 --> 00:04:57.640
But then, after I got locked up,

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:59.530
he ended up dying.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.370
So, I didn't have nothing
to do with that. (laughs)

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.900
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.780
And what emotions does
this all bring up for you?

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.753
Do you struggle with like
depression or anger or anxiety?

00:05:10.984 --> 00:05:11.950
- [Lee] A little bit of both.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.960
Depression, anger on account of,

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.623
like I said, I ain't seen
my kids since '84, so.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.580
- [Interviewer] And how
is your relationship

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.900
with your daughter,

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.870
or with the rest of your family?

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.570
- [Lee] Well, my daughter and my son,

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.910
we got along good.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:33.283
I mean, like a father and kids should.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.550
My rest of my family,

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.230
we were close knit,

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.740
my sisters and brothers
until I got in trouble.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.970
And then when I went to prison,

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:47.540
they all just seem to bury off.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:50.100
I still talk to my baby
sister though once in a while.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.480
I call her up and talk to her.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.570
So, she's the only one that I talk to.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:55.820
- [Interviewer] And your,

00:05:57.297 --> 00:05:59.520
is it a daughter and a
stepdaughter that you?

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.730
- [Lee] It's my daughter and my niece.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:02.980
- [Interviewer] And your niece.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.640
Do you have any contact with them?

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.570
- [Lee] No.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.403
- [Interviewer] Not at all?

00:06:07.403 --> 00:06:08.300
- [Lee] None at all.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.293
- [Interviewer] Since that incident,

00:06:10.293 --> 00:06:11.380
have you spoken?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:12.830
- Nope.
- Never?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.663
- [Lee] 'Cause like I said,

00:06:13.663 --> 00:06:15.000
I hadn't seen 'em since '84.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.803
That's when I got locked.

00:06:16.803 --> 00:06:19.630
- [Interviewer] I mean,
if your niece and daughter

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:24.360
knew you were not the not the predator,

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.193
you'd think they would have

00:06:25.193 --> 00:06:26.060
reached out to you at some point.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.880
- No, they done what their mama said.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.970
'Cause, just like I said,

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.100
they were 10 year old.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.210
My daughter was.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.720
And my niece was nine.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.110
So, they got together,

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:38.600
my wife, my sister-in-law

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.023
and my other sister-in-law,

00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:43.368
and they come up with
that to get a divorce.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:48.040
- [Interviewer] Did they say
in court that you were guilty?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.660
- Well, I took a no contest,

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:54.820
no contest plea 'cause I told my lawyer,

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.140
I said, "I don't want to put
my kids through any trouble.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.581
I know how these here courts do 'em,

00:06:59.581 --> 00:07:01.470
and they cross examine and all this.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:04.470
And I said, "They're too young for that."

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:07.690
So I went ahead and took a
plea bargain just like I said.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.040
I've done 15 years in prisons,

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.870
and 19 up there at Arcadia

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.550
in that there sexual rehabilitating,

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.653
- [Interviewer] Yeah, and
how'd you take to the therapy?

00:07:24.095 --> 00:07:24.928
- Eh.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.080
I made it through it, you know?

00:07:31.113 --> 00:07:33.115
- [Interviewer] What kind
of things did they work on?

00:07:33.115 --> 00:07:34.980
- Well, they work on your attitudes,

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:38.010
your sexual thoughts

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:39.183
and things like that.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.858
- [Interviewer] And yet you

00:07:44.858 --> 00:07:47.230
had another marriage after this, right?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.860
- Yes.
- When you got out of prison?

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.680
- Well, not when I got out of prison.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:52.910
Well, I got out,

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.423
and then I had to go back
on a violation of probation.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.210
But, let's see,

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.020
my second marriage,

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.113
we got married in '80,

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.963
let's see '84?

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.033
No, '80, '90?

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.443
About '90, '91.

00:08:13.443 --> 00:08:15.017
Then we got a divorce in '92,

00:08:15.017 --> 00:08:17.913
and never went back on the
violation of probation.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.642
- [Interviewer] What lesson
has this all taught you?

00:08:22.642 --> 00:08:23.630
- Huh?

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:25.503
- [Interviewer] What have
you learned from all of this?

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.550
- I learned to be careful
who I mess with. (laughing)

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.230
Very careful.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:33.063
- [Interviewer] What are you doing now?

00:08:33.063 --> 00:08:34.180
Are you staying away from kids?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.013
- Yes.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.130
- [Interviewer] And do you
have any friends today?

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:39.963
- Oh yeah.

00:08:39.963 --> 00:08:41.600
I've got a girlfriend now.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.483
I was just with her a
while before you come.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.345
- [Interviewer] And
looking back at your life,

00:08:50.345 --> 00:08:51.545
do you have any regrets?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:53.790
- Looking back at it?

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.780
Yes, I have regrets 'cause I regret

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.730
that I was accused of something
that I didn't do, you know?

00:09:03.158 --> 00:09:04.330
- [Interviewer] What would
you have done differently

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.950
if you could?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.510
- Well, if I could go back

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.203
and do things over,

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.683
I don't think I'd ever
gotten married. (laughs)

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:18.150
Just on account of the way
the first wife treated me.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:20.853
So.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.220
'Cause I was a virgin there.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.460
Me and her got married,

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.350
and just like I said,

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:29.130
after my son was born in '76,

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.007
we didn't have sex,

00:09:30.007 --> 00:09:32.660
but we was together for about 15 year.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.923
14, 15 year.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:38.683
- [Interviewer] All right Lee.

00:09:38.683 --> 00:09:40.430
Well, thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.263
- You're welcome.

00:09:41.263 --> 00:09:42.620
- [Interviewer] And I wish
you and your girlfriend

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:44.120
the best of luck.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.481
- Well, this here gal,

00:09:45.481 --> 00:09:47.583
lady that I'm going with,

00:09:48.725 --> 00:09:51.680
I think she's just a few
years younger than me.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.650
She was born in '52 I think, or '53.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:59.150
So, we seem to be hitting
it off pretty good.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.220
- [Interviewer] Good luck with that.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:01.053
- Oh yeah.

00:10:01.053 --> 00:10:01.886
- [Interviewer] All right.

00:10:01.886 --> 00:10:02.790
Thank you Lee.
- Oh yes.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.840
- Okay.
- Thank you.

